.TH TREK 1 "October 2026" "trek 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
trek \- a graphical file manager driven with vim motions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trek
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.RI [ FILE | URI ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B trek
is a graphical file manager driven from the keyboard with vim motions:
the parent folder, the files and a preview side by side, a cursor
moved with h, j, k and l, and a selection built with Space or visual mode.
Press ~ or F1 in the window for the list of keys.
It began as a port of PCManFM to Rust and GTK 4, and keeps PCManFM's menus,
view modes, tabs, dual pane, side pane, trash can, volume handling and
dialogs.
.PP
Folders named on the command line open as tabs in the window that was last
used, or in a new window when there is none; files are opened with their
applications.
.B ~
means the home folder, and a relative path is resolved against the
directory the command was run from.
With no arguments, that directory is opened in a new window.
.PP
One instance runs for each profile; a second invocation hands its arguments
to the first and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-profile =\fIPROFILE\fR
Use the settings of
.I PROFILE
(default:
.BR default ).
Each profile is its own instance.
Only honoured by the first instance of a profile.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemon\-mode
Start without a window and keep running after the last window is closed.
Only honoured by the first instance.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-new\-win
Open the folders in a new window instead of in tabs.
.TP
.BR \-\-show\-pref =\fIN\fR
Open Preferences at page
.IR N :
1 General, 2 Display, 3 Layout, 4 Volume Management, 5 Advanced.
.TP
.B \-\-import\-pcmanfm
Read the settings of PCManFM and libfm, take over those
.B trek
has, save them to the profile, print what was and was not imported, and
exit.
The files read are
.I ~/.config/pcmanfm/PROFILE/pcmanfm.conf
(or PCManFM's
.B default
profile when there is none of that name) and
.IR ~/.config/libfm/libfm.conf ;
they are not changed.
This is never done automatically.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-desktop ", " \-\-role =\fIROLE\fR
Accepted for compatibility with PCManFM and Nautilus; they do nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options; what follows is a file name even if it starts with a dash.
.PP
PCManFM's desktop and search options
.RB ( \-\-desktop ,
.BR \-\-desktop\-off ,
.BR \-\-desktop\-pref ,
.BR \-\-one\-screen ,
.BR \-\-set\-wallpaper ,
.BR \-\-wallpaper\-mode ,
.BR \-\-find\-files )
are recognised and refused with a message: this version has no desktop
manager and no Find Files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
.B \-\-import\-pcmanfm
found nothing to import, or could not read it.
.TP
.B 2
An option was not understood.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERMINAL
The terminal emulator to use when none is set in Preferences.
.TP
.B TREK_ALLOW_ROOTS
When set, confines copying, moving, deleting, renaming and creating files
to the folders it lists (a semicolon-separated list of paths or URIs),
the test fixture
.RI ( ~/.cache/trek\-fixture )
and the temporary directory.
Unset, files may be changed anywhere.
.TP
.B TREK_GTK_THEME
The name of the GTK theme to follow, for a session that cannot tell which
one the desktop uses.
.TP
.B TREK_TRACE
Set to
.B 1
to print start-up and folder-loading times on standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/trek/PROFILE/trek.conf
Settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/trek/PROFILE/dir\-settings.conf
View settings of folders that have "Preserve This Folder's Settings" on.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gtk\-3.0/bookmarks
Bookmarks, shared with GTK file choosers and other file managers.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/thumbnails
Thumbnails, shared with other programs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pcmanfm (1),
.BR gio (1),
.BR xdg\-mime (1)
